- TODO: statistical review of Chapter 2 - How sure can I be?
    - Date: 2026-04-30
    - Summary: Most Loop D rejection-rate numbers in the prose disagree with the saved simulation grid (and with the theoretical exact-binomial powers). Several pedagogical traps need tightening: the "5% combined" tail figure, the "tracks almost perfectly at N=100" claim (the comparison conflates a two-sided p-value with a one-sided posterior), the Beta(2,8) edge case which contradicts itself, the "type I rate equals alpha" line (the exact binomial test is conservative, ~3.3% at N=50), and the soft "Bayesian is sure that p sits inside a particular interval" framing.
    - Items
        - HIGH (applied): Loop D rejection rates in the prose do not match the saved grid `data/rejection_rates_grid.npy` or theory. Saved grid (rows = p in [0.50,0.52,0.55,0.60], cols = N in [50,200,1000]):
            - p=0.50: 3.1%, 4.0%, 4.6%   (prose says "roughly 5% at every N")
            - p=0.52: 4.2%, 6.8%, 23.1%  (prose says 6%, 8%, 18%)
            - p=0.55: 8.2%, 25.7%, 88.0% (prose says 8%, 25%, 86%)
